freeglut demos for riscos-mesa
==============================

These are demos from freeglut 3.8.0 (progs/demos), built unchanged against
riscos-mesa's freeglut. freeglut is the open source GLUT: the small library
most OpenGL example programs, tutorials and books use to open a window and
read the keyboard and mouse. riscos-mesa's freeglut has a native RISC OS
back end:

- each GLUT window is a Wimp window (subwindows are drawn inside it), and
  the programs multitask;
- GLUT menus are Wimp menus: click Menu over a window that has one
  (Select or Adjust too, if the program attached the menu to them). A
  choice made with Adjust leaves the menu open;
- drawing goes through riscos-mesa's EGL and software OpenGL 2.1;
- full screen and game mode cover the desktop with a window without a
  title bar, in the current screen mode.

Mouse buttons: Select is GLUT's left button, Menu the middle one and
Adjust the right one, as on the mouse.

!Shapes    every GLUT shape; Page Up / Page Down change the shape
!One       two windows, nested subwindows, menus and game mode (Escape
           leaves game mode)
!Subwin    nested subwindows; typing goes to the one under the pointer
!Lorenz    the Lorenz attractor
!Fractals  an affine fractal (Koch snowflake)
!Resizer   moving, resizing, hiding and showing windows from the keyboard
!View3D    a lit scene; drag with Select to turn it, F1 for help
!Keyboard  shows the keys (and special keys, with Shift/Ctrl/Alt) held

Text the programs print goes to the file Output inside each application.

The programs need SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (from PackMan) and a
machine with VFPv4 (Raspberry Pi 2 or later and similar). Each application
includes freeglut's licence (MIT/X style).

To build your own GLUT programs, see docs/porting/glut.md in riscos-mesa.
